<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A stand-in for https://archlinux.org/feeds/news/, used by synpkg_test.sh
  through SYNPKG_NEWS_FILE.

  SYNTHETIC ON PURPOSE, rather than a saved copy of the real feed. The dates
  here are fixed, so a test can assert "one item is newer than this cutoff" and
  still mean it in a year. A saved copy would drift out from under the
  assertions the moment Arch published anything, and the honest fix for that is
  a test that asserts nothing.

  It also carries the shapes the parser has to survive, which a real feed only
  sometimes contains: a CDATA payload, escaped HTML inside a description,
  named and numeric entities, a token with no spaces in it (the wrapper's
  hard-split path), and an item with no pubDate at all.

  SynapseOS Project — GPL-2.0-or-later
-->
<rss version="2.0">
  <channel>
    <title>Arch Linux: Recent news updates</title>
    <link>https://archlinux.org/news/</link>

    <item>
      <title>gizmo &gt;= 2.0 requires manual intervention</title>
      <link>https://example.invalid/news/gizmo-2-0/</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;gizmo&lt;/code&gt; package now ships a file that was previously untracked. Run &lt;code&gt;pacman -Syu --overwrite &apos;/usr/lib/gizmo/*&apos;&lt;/code&gt; once.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A very long unbreakable token follows: /usr/lib/gizmo/aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 09:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>

